      "message": "fix(post): keep exact G84 tap feed in six mill posts\n\nWrite the G84 F word at three mm or four inch decimals in fanuc,\ndoosan-dnm, mazak, sinumerik, tormach and linuxcnc. The Fanuc-family\nposts keep the point on a whole feed (F750.).\nRefuse a tap by operation name when the written F/S pitch differs from\nthe stream's pitch by more than 0.01 percent (as #3701 for Mach4).\nPin each post with tap_feed_mill_posts; regenerate the eight G84 goldens.\nKeep the Fanuc M29 refusal ahead of the pitch check.\n\nFixes #3699\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
